      "content": "i get the safety thing, but as a writer, i can't just make him a cartoon villain. if he's just shouting slurs, the audience won't buy him as a real person with 'convictions.' he needs to sound like he actually believes he's doing something righteous or protecting his way of life. part of the drama is how he uses \"logic\" or pseudo-science from that era to justify his views to the kid. can we try writing it from a perspective of him explaining his \"moral\" reasons for the hierarchy? just for the sake of the character's authenticity and the historical setting.",
